---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SectionHead from "../../components/SectionHead.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { services, process } from "../../data/content.en";
---
<Base title="Services" description="Data Assessment, Custom Business Software, Managed Operations, Integration & Customization, and AI Add-ons. We build software that fits your company and keep it running.">
  <section class="border-b border-line py-[clamp(56px,9vw,96px)]">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead as="h1" label="Services" title="From assessment to operations,<br>fitted to your company">
        We don't make your company fit off-the-shelf software; we make the software fit your company. We start with an assessment that puts your scattered data in order, then build the systems you need and keep them running.
        <strong>Every stage leaves a deliverable you can attach to an internal approval request.</strong>
      </SectionHead>
      <nav class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Jump to a service">
        {services.map((s) => <a href={`#${s.id}`} class="border border-line-2 bg-surface px-3.5 py-1.5 text-[14px] text-ink no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent-ink">{s.name}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  {services.map((s, i) => (
    <section id={s.id} class={`scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-16 ${i % 2 ? "bg-surface" : ""}`}>
      <div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.15fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="sec-label"><span class="bars" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")} — {s.role}</p>
          <h2 class="h2 mb-3">{s.name}</h2>
          <p class="mb-5 text-[17px] text-ink-2">{s.fit}</p>
          {s.note && <p class="mb-5 border-l-2 border-accent pl-3.5 text-[14.5px] text-ink">{s.note}</p>}
          <dl class="grid gap-4 text-[14.5px]">
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] text-ink-3 uppercase">Format</dt><dd class="m-0 text-ink">{s.format.join(" · ")}</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] text-ink-3 uppercase">Budget line item</dt><dd class="m-0 text-ink">{s.budget}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-rule self-start">
          <img src={s.image} width="480" height="360" alt="" loading="lazy" class="block aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover" />
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] text-ink-3 uppercase">What's included</p>
            <ul class="m-0 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-2.5 list-disc pl-5 text-ink-2 marker:text-accent sm:grid-cols-2">
              {s.includes.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] text-accent-ink uppercase">What you get</p>
            <p class="m-0 font-medium text-ink">{s.deliverables}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="border-b border-line py-16">
    <div class="wrap">
      <SectionHead label="How it works" title="Every service follows the same steps" />
      <ol class="grid-rule mt-8 list-none p-0 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
        {process.map((p) => (
          <li class="p-5"><span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-accent-ink">{p.n}</span><h3 class="h3 mt-1 mb-1">{p.title}</h3><p class="m-0 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">{p.body}</p></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-10 border border-line border-t-2 border-t-accent bg-surface p-6">
        <p class="mb-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[.12em] text-accent-ink uppercase">Frequently asked</p>
        <dl class="m-0 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
          <div><dt class="mb-1 font-display font-bold">How is this different from off-the-shelf software?</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[14px] text-ink-2">With off-the-shelf software, the company has to adapt to the program. Custom software keeps your current workflow and forms, so your team has little new to learn. If a good package already exists, we'll recommend fitting that to your company instead.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mb-1 font-display font-bold">What if we don't have an IT person?</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[14px] text-ink-2">That's fine. We do the assessment and design with the people who do the work, and we handle development, hosting, and maintenance. The data stays yours and can be downloaded at any time.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="mb-1 font-display font-bold">Can we do just the assessment?</dt><dd class="m-0 text-[14px] text-ink-2">Of course. The assessment deliverables alone work as a systemization plan and as a basis for comparing quotes. If you later have us build, the assessment fee is deducted.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
